WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.620
One river supports our homes, farms, and nature.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.140
Every decision matters.

3
00:00:11.266 --> 00:00:14.446
A basin is land that drains towards a shared river.

4
00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:17.666
Rain runs downhill, or soaks into the ground.

5
00:00:23.126 --> 00:00:27.226
Clean water supports our homes, our food, our energy, and the life
around us.

6
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:37.683
When water runs low, families, farms, and wildlife all feel the
pressure.

7
00:00:47.349 --> 00:00:50.229
Heavy rain can carry soil and pollution downstream.

8
00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:53.049
What happens upstream affects others below.

9
00:00:58.495 --> 00:01:03.005
Collect wastewater, treat it, and check its quality before release or
safe reuse.

10
00:01:10.095 --> 00:01:12.455
Protect riverbanks and keep soil covered.

11
00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:14.505
Give nature room to recover.

12
00:01:20.332 --> 00:01:25.772
Wetlands can slow floodwater, trap sediment, and shelter wildlife. Keep
space for them.

13
00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:36.112
Use water wisely. Treat wastewater. Protect wetlands. We all have a part
to play.

14
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:45.450
We developed Riverkeeper, a game for practising real-world watershed
management.

15
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.100
Try different choices.

16
00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:57.400
Balance water, food, energy and nature, and learn from the results.

17
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.150
Now, put these ideas into practice with Riverkeeper.

18
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:04.910
Your choices shape the basin.

19
00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:06.250
Let's see how to play.

20
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:15.560
This is the Mahaweli River Basin. Your role is to manage it sustainably
over twenty-four months.

21
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:22.500
Balance your funds, water, food and energy with community wellbeing and
a healthy environment.

22
00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.330
Choose developments and policies.

23
00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:27.610
Prepare for droughts and heavy rain.

24
00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:31.400
Review each month's results, and improve your plan.

25
00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:36.150
First, explore your basin.

26
00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.170
Drag to rotate the map, and scroll to zoom.

27
00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:40.830
Right-drag to move.

28
00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:45.810
Switch on sub-basin boundaries and numbers to find the places mentioned
by Bindu.

29
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.530
Let's read the resource bar.

30
00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.010
Funds are your development budget.

31
00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.790
Population shows the people you support.

32
00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.870
Water serves people and nature.

33
00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.310
Food keeps communities supplied.

34
00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:01.870
Electricity powers the basin.

35
00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.690
Wellbeing reflects people's needs.

36
00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.850
Ecology tracks ecosystem health.

37
00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.210
And your score measures overall success.

38
00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:13.210
Ready to build?

39
00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.530
Open the building tools and select a hexagon.

40
00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.870
Choose a category, then select a development.

41
00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:22.330
Let's try solar power.

42
00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.090
Review the price and predicted effects.

43
00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.090
When you're ready, choose Place development.

44
00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:29.890
There it is!

45
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.410
Your funds pay for the new site.

46
00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:36.810
Plan a balanced mix of housing, food, energy and nature.

47
00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.570
Hydropower needs a suitable river location.

48
00:03:40.883 --> 00:03:41.903
Now open Water.

49
00:03:42.703 --> 00:03:49.103
Check local needs, then adjust allocations for communities, farms,
industry and river ecosystems.

50
00:03:50.143 --> 00:03:53.163
In this example, we increase the river's allocation.

51
00:03:53.963 --> 00:03:58.983
Keep water available for nature, while checking that each community
receives what it needs.

52
00:04:00.016 --> 00:04:02.616
Improve the sites you already have.

53
00:04:03.336 --> 00:04:05.756
Select a farm and review its policies.

54
00:04:06.556 --> 00:04:09.536
Here, we choose contour strips and soil cover.

55
00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:14.496
Check the installation and monthly costs, then apply the policy.

56
00:04:15.556 --> 00:04:18.936
Better soil protection helps reduce environmental pressure.

57
00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:20.550
Think ahead!

58
00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.390
Read Bindu's advice and the basin outlook.

59
00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.830
A heavy-rain warning is your chance to prepare before the rain arrives.

60
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:33.030
Protect vulnerable land, review your water plan, and keep useful
reserves.

61
00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.010
Preparation makes your basin stronger.

62
00:04:37.016 --> 00:04:38.176
Ready for the next month?

63
00:04:38.916 --> 00:04:39.876
Select the large arrow.

64
00:04:40.656 --> 00:04:41.736
Then open Month results.

65
00:04:42.656 --> 00:04:47.256
Review the benefits, penalties and resource changes before making your
next decisions.

66
00:04:48.136 --> 00:04:49.916
Success is more than money.

67
00:04:50.336 --> 00:04:54.956
Support people, maintain useful resources, and protect healthy
ecosystems.

68
00:04:56.383 --> 00:04:59.843
Complete all twenty-four months to reveal your final score.

69
00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:04.963
Sign in to save an account campaign and compare eligible completed
scores.

70
00:05:05.883 --> 00:05:06.483
Your basin.

71
00:05:07.043 --> 00:05:07.643
Your decisions.

72
00:05:08.623 --> 00:05:10.163
Let's build a better future!
